source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: Jira forms no link at all when a bracket body spans a physical line: it renders the markup as text with a line break. jiro's own bracket scan still reads across the line, a pre-existing divergence for every part of the body, and it reads the title as one line the way it reads every other inline run; a JFM title jiro writes to Jira is therefore flattened to one line with a warning.
-- input.jira --
[y|http://y|a
b]
-- rendered.html --
<p>[y|http://y|a<br/>
b]</p>
-- want.md --
[y](http://y "a b")
-- warnings.json --
[]
